<title>BRAZIL: Brazil net dollar inflows at $74.7 mln May 20.</title>
<headline>Brazil net dollar inflows at $74.7 mln May 20.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-05-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Preliminary figures for Brazil's commercial and financial foreign exchange contracts showed a $74.7 million surplus on May 20 in the commercial forex market, according to Central Bank data suplied to banks.</p>
<p>A banker with access to the figures said the Central Bank issued the following breakdown.</p>
<p>DOLLAR FLOWS ON MAY 20</p>
<p>Exports: $335.4 million</p>
<p>Imports: $282.2 million</p>
<p>Finanancial buy: $225.4 million</p>
<p>Financial sell: $203.9 million</p>
<p>Net surplus: $74.7 million</p>
<p>MAY DOLLAR FLOWS UP DATE</p>
<p>Exports: $3.433 billion</p>
<p>Imports: $3.299 billion</p>
<p>Financial buy: $4.334 billion</p>
<p>Financial sell: $3.254 billion</p>
<p>Net surplus: $1.214 billion</p>
<p>Note: Figures rounded off.</p>
<p>((--Alexandre Caverni, Sao Paulo newsroon, 55 11 2485418))</p>
